{
  "title": "Calorie architecture phase 3: store shopping-list categories at write instead of touching every item on catalog changes",
  "description": "Phase 3 of the design in doc/calorie-estimates.md (\"Architecture\"), approved 2026-10-11. \
Shopping categories are computed on every read (server/src/api/shopping_list/list.rs computed_category, sync.rs), so incremental sync only sends a new category if the item's row changes. \
To get catalog edits to clients, startup runs touch_recategorized_items, which bumps every live item whose categorizer_version differs from ramekin_core::ingredient_categorizer::version(). \
Any catalog edit changes that version, so every client re-syncs its whole list after a deploy. \
Approved design: store the computed category on the shopping item when it's written (create, update that renames, sync). \
Recompute and touch only the items whose name just got resolved (ingredient_names::save_resolved and sync_with_catalog already touch those items). \
Catalog deploys don't touch existing items; better categories reach new items. \
Delete touch_recategorized_items and its startup call, stop reading and writing categorizer_version, and drop ingredient_categorizer::version() and catalog::version() if nothing else uses them. \
Keep the categorizer_version column (see blocked-calorie-drop-dead-columns). \
A migration backfills the stored category for live items. \
Both web and iOS already read category from the server; check that neither needs a change. \
Add e2e coverage that a catalog-independent item keeps its stored category and that resolving a name updates and re-syncs only that item.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
  "type": "task",
